@layout.app({ title: 'Terms and Conditions' })
  @slot('meta')
    <meta name="description" content="The terms for using the nvp.gg URL shortener." />
  @endslot
  
  <div class="ember-primitives__hero__wrapper">
    <div class="hero-content">
      <h1>
        Terms and Conditions
      </h1>
      <em>Last updated: September 21, 2026</em>
    </div>
  </div>

  <main class="legal">
    <h2 id="gist">
      The gist
    </h2>
    <p>
      nvp.gg shortens URLs. These terms describe what you can expect from us and what we expect
      from you. Read them. If you do not agree to them, do not use the Service.
    </p>
    <p>
      Short version: do not shorten links to anything illegal, harmful, or deceptive. Keep your
      account secure. Paid plans renew monthly until you cancel. The Service comes as is.
    </p>

    <h2 id="who">
      1. Who's who
    </h2>
    <p>
      "We" and "us" mean NullVoxPopuli, who runs nvp.gg. "You" means anyone who uses the Service.
      The "Service" means nvp.gg, api.nvp.gg, docs.nvp.gg, and every short link they serve. If you
      use the Service for a company or another person, you confirm that you can accept these
      terms for them.
    </p>

    <h2 id="account">
      2. Your account
    </h2>
    <p>
      You sign in with GitHub. You are responsible for everything done with your account, your
      API keys, and your team accounts. Keep your keys secret. Tell us at once if you believe
      someone else has used your account. If we believe your account is compromised, we can
      suspend it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
      explains what we do with the information you give
      us.
    </p>

    <h2 id="age">
      3. Minimum age
    </h2>
    <p>
      You must be at least 13 years old, or 16 in the European Economic Area, to use the Service.
      If you are under 18, you can use it only with a parent or guardian who agrees to these terms.
    </p>

    <h2 id="links">
      4. Your links
    </h2>
    <p>
      You are responsible for every URL you shorten and every domain you attach. You must not use
      the Service to link to, or to spread:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        malware, phishing pages, or anything that steals credentials or data;
      </li>
      <li>
        spam, or links sent in bulk to people who did not ask for them;
      </li>
      <li>
        content that is illegal where you or the visitor live;
      </li>
      <li>
        content that infringes someone's copyright, trademark, or privacy;
      </li>
      <li>
        content that harasses, threatens, or exploits people;
      </li>
      <li>
        anything that hides the true destination to deceive the visitor.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not review links before they go live, and we cannot review all of them afterwards. We
      can disable or delete any link, and suspend any account, that we believe breaks these rules,
      without notice.
    </p>
    <p>
      Short links are public. Anyone with the link can open it. Deleting a link stops it from
      resolving, but copies of the short URL can remain elsewhere.
    </p>

    <h2 id="fees">
      5. Fees, payment, and renewal
    </h2>
    <p>
      Some features need a paid plan. The plans and prices are on the
      <a href="https://nvp.gg/pricing">pricing page</a>. Stripe processes payment. By starting a
      plan you allow us and Stripe to charge the card you provide.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Plans are billed monthly and renew automatically until you cancel.
      </li>
      <li>
        Cancel any time through the billing portal. Access continues until the end of the period you paid for.
      </li>
      <li>
        We do not refund a partial period, unless the law where you live requires it.
      </li>
      <li>
        If a payment fails, we can downgrade the account to the free allowance until it succeeds.
      </li>
      <li>
        Plan limits, such as links per month, apply as described on the pricing page. We can change prices and plans, with notice before the next renewal.
      </li>
      <li>
        You are responsible for any taxes that apply to your purchase.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="api">
      6. The API
    </h2>
    <p>
      You can use the Service through its API with an API key. Keys are limited to the scopes and
      the account they were created for. Do not share keys or use them to get around plan limits or
      rate limits. We can revoke keys and change rate limits to protect the Service.
    </p>

    <h2 id="domains">
      7. Custom domains
    </h2>
    <p>
      You can only attach a domain that you own or control. You are responsible for its DNS and for
      its content. We can remove a domain that you do not control or that is used against these
      terms.
    </p>

    <h2 id="teams">
      8. Teams
    </h2>
    <p>
      The admin of a team account is responsible for the account, its billing, its members, and
      its links. Members can see and manage the account's links. An admin can remove a member at
      any time.
    </p>

    <h2 id="feedback">
      9. Feedback
    </h2>
    <p>
      If you send us ideas or suggestions, we can use them without owing you anything.
    </p>

    <h2 id="ip">
      10. Intellectual property
    </h2>
    <p>
      The source code of the Service is published under the GNU AGPL v3 license on
      <a href="https://github.com/NullVoxPopuli/url-shortener">GitHub</a>. That license covers the
      code. It does not cover the nvp.gg name, the domains, or the hosted Service. You keep every
      right to the URLs and content you link to.
    </p>

    <h2 id="third-party">
      11. Third-party services
    </h2>
    <p>
      The Service uses GitHub for sign-in and Stripe for payment. Their terms apply to your use of
      them. We are not responsible for third-party services, or for the sites your short links go
      to.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">
      12. Changes
    </h2>
    <p>
      We can change these terms, for example when the Service changes or the law changes. When we
      do, we update the date at the top. If a change is material, we will also say so on the site.
      Changes apply from the date they are posted. If you keep using the Service after a change,
      you accept it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="termination">
      13. Termination
    </h2>
    <p>
      We can end or suspend your access to all or part of the Service at any time, with or without
      cause or notice, including when we believe you broke these terms. We can also reclaim short
      codes or domains after long inactivity. You can stop using the Service at any time, and you
      can cancel a paid plan as described in section 5.
    </p>

    <h2 id="disclaimers">
      14. Disclaimers
    </h2>
    <p>
      The Service is provided "as is", to the extent the law allows. We make no warranty that it
      will be error free, uninterrupted, or that short links will resolve forever. You use it at
      your own risk.
    </p>

    <h2 id="law">
      15. Jurisdiction and applicable law
    </h2>
    <p>
      Except where the law says otherwise, these terms and your use of the Service are governed by
      the laws of the United States and of the State of
      <!-- Set the state where the operator resides before publishing. -->
      [State], without regard to conflict of law rules, and disputes go to the state and federal
      courts of that state. Nothing here removes rights you have as a consumer under the law where
      you live.
    </p>

    <h2 id="liability">
      16. Limitation of liability
    </h2>
    <p>
      To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for special, incidental, or consequential
      damages, for the cost of substitute services, for lost or corrupted data, or for any amount
      above the greater of $50 and the fees you paid us in the twelve months before the claim.
      For consumers in Europe, our liability is limited to the maximum the law of your country
      allows, and this section does not limit liability for death, personal injury, willful
      misconduct, or gross negligence.
    </p>

    <h2 id="indemnification">
      17. Indemnification
    </h2>
    <p>
      You agree to defend us against, and cover, any claim, loss, or cost, including reasonable
      legal fees, that arises from your use of the Service, from the links you create, or from
      your breach of these terms.
    </p>

    <h2 id="misc">
      18. Miscellaneous
    </h2>
    <p>
      These terms are the whole agreement between you and us about the Service. If a part of them
      is unenforceable, the rest still applies. If we do not enforce a term once, we can still
      enforce it later. We can assign these terms. You can assign them only with our written
      consent. These terms are written in English, and the English version controls.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">
      Contact
    </h2>
    <p>
      Open an issue on
      <a href="https://github.com/NullVoxPopuli/url-shortener">GitHub</a>
      or ask in the Discord linked in the footer.
    </p>

    <p class="attribution">
      Adapted from
      <a href="https://github.com/Automattic/legalmattic">Automattic's Legalmattic</a>
      terms of service, under the
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">Creative Commons BY-SA 4.0</a>
      license. These terms are available under the same license.
    </p>
  </main>
@end
